<h1>Running Folder Parameter test</h1>
<p>Unlike the <a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/running-hello-world-test/">Hello World test</a>, this test
  can't just be run as-is: its <code>maze_executable_folder</code> parameter is
  <a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/adding-configuration-parameter/#config-class">required</a> and has no
  meaningful default, so a value has to be supplied before the test can do anything.</p>

<h2 id="running-from-cli">Running from CLI</h2>
<h3 id="required-field-unset-error">Required field unset error</h3>
<p>Running the test file as-is fails, because the required folder was never set:</p>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("python test_folder_parameter.py") }}
<p>With no folder to run the executable from, the case ends in an
  <a class="text-accent" href="/framework/statuses/#statuses"><strong class="text-warning">ERROR</strong></a>
  status, and the reason is carried into both the case's and the test's
  <a class="text-accent" href="/framework/result-fields/">result tables</a>:</p>
{% ansiOutput "folder-parameter-run-failed.ansi" %}
<p>To run it from the CLI, set the parameter's <a class="text-accent" href="/framework/configuration-fields/#options"><code>default</code></a>
  in the config class to the folder you downloaded the Maze application into:</p>
{{ codeblock.block('	maze_executable_folder = OrcraftConfigField.Folder(
		default=r"C:\\Orcraft\\Maze\\bin\\v3.0.0",
		label="Maze Executable Folder",
		required=True,
	)') }}
<p>Now the test has a value to work with when run directly, without changing anything else.</p>

<h3 id="pass-run-output">Pass run output</h3>
<p>With a valid folder, the test runs the Maze executable and logs its output as part of the test's own log:</p>
{% ansiOutput "folder-parameter-run.ansi" %}
<p>Notice the <strong>Maze Executable Folder</strong> column in the configuration table - every config parameter
  a test declares shows up there, so the log always records exactly what the test was run with. The indented
  block in the middle is the Maze application's own stdout, captured and logged by the test.</p>
<p>We could keep this default as is, if as test developers we want whoever executes the test to always start from
  this folder. For demonstration purposes, though, let's reset it back to an empty default:</p>
{{ codeblock.block('	maze_executable_folder = OrcraftConfigField.Folder(
		default="",
		label="Maze Executable Folder",
		required=True,
	)') }}

<h2 id="running-from-gui">Running from GUI</h2>
<p>Let's click on the <strong>Folder Parameter</strong> test. Its configuration tab now shows the
  <strong>Maze Executable Folder</strong> field alongside the built-in <code>Cycles</code> field we met earlier.
  You can see the field is empty and marked in <strong class="text-orange">orange</strong> - meaning it's a
  required field that isn't set:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-folder-parameter-test/gui-empty.png", "Folder Parameter test selected in the Orcraft controller, with its empty required Maze Executable Folder field marked in orange", "large") }}
<h3 id="missing-argument">Missing argument</h3>
<p>If we click <strong class="text-purple">Run</strong> now, we'll see a warning regarding the missing arguments:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-folder-parameter-test/missing-arguments.png", "Missing Arguments dialog in the Orcraft controller, listing Maze Executable Folder as a required argument", "large") }}

<h3 id="setting-the-folder">Setting the folder</h3>
<p>Let's click <strong>Browse</strong> and select version <strong>2.0.0</strong> of the Maze app to test it:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-folder-parameter-test/browse-for-maze-folder.png", "Browse dialog in the Orcraft controller with the Maze app's v2.0.0 folder selected", "large") }}
<p>As you can see now, the field changed from its default, but is unplanned yet. Remember the details from the
  <a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/editing-run-configuration/#field-and-badge-legend">Editing run
  configuration chapter's summary</a>:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-folder-parameter-test/maze-folder-selected.png", "Maze Executable Folder field set to the v2.0.0 folder in the Orcraft controller, shown in purple with an orange dot indicating an unplanned change", "large") }}
<p>We can run it as unplanned, but we'll click <strong class="text-accent">Update Plan</strong>:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-folder-parameter-test/update-plan-clicked.png", "Maze Executable Folder field shown in blue after clicking Update Plan in the Orcraft controller", "large") }}

<h3 id="running-the-test">Running the test</h3>
<p>Let's click <strong class="text-purple">Run</strong> and see the same log we saw earlier from the CLI - note
  that here we ran with the <strong>v2.0.0</strong> folder, while in the CLI we ran with the default
  <strong>v3.0.0</strong>:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/running-folder-parameter-test/run-result.png", "Log tab of the Folder Parameter test run in the Orcraft controller, showing the same output as the CLI run", "large") }}
